<%# role="status": the strip appears without anybody asking for it, so it has to
    say so once. Polite, i.e. it waits for a pause -- an offer is not an alert.

    The fixed ids are safe here for the same reason they were safe in the shell,
    and it is worth stating rather than assuming (this feature has hit the
    duplicate-id trap three times, the last one in production, #612): this
    component renders ONLY into assistant_panel_body, and that frame exists once
    per document. The take button points at whichever sentence is showing via
    aria-describedby, which is what the ids are for.

    A card and no longer a full-bleed bar: in the shell it spanned the panel and
    sat on its own tinted ground because it was pinned to the bottom edge. Inside
    the frame it is one block in the writing zone, so it takes that zone's
    shape -- the same rounded, quiet outline the message field below it uses. %>
<div data-assistant-panel-target="offer"
     role="status"
     class="hidden mb-2 rounded-2xl border border-cream-300 bg-cream-100 px-3 py-2 text-xs">
  <%# flex-wrap, and a floor under the label: every other child is shrink-0, so
      the label is the only thing that can give way, and at
      AssistantPanelState::MIN_WIDTH (280px) the fixed chrome eats the whole row
      -- without a floor the strip read "Bezug wechseln zu: [nothing]
      Uebernehmen". The buttons drop to a second line instead of squeezing out
      the one piece of information the strip exists to carry.

      The floor is 4rem and no longer 7rem: the strip used to span the shell and
      now sits inside the frame's padding, roughly 56px narrower, and at 7rem the
      dismiss button wrapped to a line of its own at the DEFAULT width -- a
      second line carrying nothing but an x. Measured at 380px: the fixed parts
      leave about 5rem, so 4rem keeps one line and still refuses to truncate the
      title into nothing. %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <i class="bi bi-stars shrink-0 text-cream-500" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <%# Two lead sentences rather than one that JavaScript rewrites: the FIRST
        reference and a further one are different acts, and a translation is the
        server's to write. Only the ticket's own title is filled in by the
        controller, and that is data from the page, not a translation.

        ⚠️ The second one said "Bezug wechseln zu" until S2, and it was accurate
        then: with a limit of one, taking the offer replaced what stood there.
        With ten it ADDS, so the sentence, the key and the target were renamed
        together -- a target called offerSwitch rendering "hinzufuegen" is the
        drift this file is full of warnings about. %>
    <span id="assistant_offer_set" data-assistant-panel-target="offerSet" class="shrink-0 text-faint"><%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.offer.set') %></span>
    <span id="assistant_offer_add" data-assistant-panel-target="offerAdd" class="hidden shrink-0 text-faint"><%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.offer.add') %></span>
    <span id="assistant_offer_label" data-assistant-panel-target="offerLabel" class="min-w-[4rem] flex-1 truncate font-semibold text-cream-900"></span>
    <%# The softened primary, not the house border-2 black: the panel's own edge
        and its "Neuer Chat" button gave that up on 27.08.2026 for the reason
        that applies here word for word -- in a quiet strip the only bordered
        surface shouts louder than everything around it. The full token comes
        back on hover. %>
    <button type="button"
            data-assistant-panel-target="offerTake"
            data-action="assistant-panel#takeOffer"
            class="shrink-0 rounded border border-stroke/30 bg-btn-primary/60 px-2 py-0.5 font-semibold text-ink transition-all hover:bg-btn-primary focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink focus-visible:ring-offset-1">
      <%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.offer.take') %>
    </button>
    <%# Sized like every other icon button in this shell (expand, collapse,
        history, close, "Neuer Chat"), not as a bare 10px glyph with 4px of side
        padding: that was an 18x10 target, well under the 24x24 the guidelines
        ask for. %>
    <button type="button"
            data-action="assistant-panel#dismissOffer"
            title="<%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.offer.dismiss') %>"
            aria-label="<%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.offer.dismiss') %>"
            class="shrink-0 w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center rounded text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:text-cream-900 hover:bg-cream-200 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink">
      <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
